<title>BELGIUM: EU cereals crop still not pinned down - Commission.</title>
<headline>EU cereals crop still not pinned down - Commission.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has no accurate figure yet but will tell the EU's cereals advisory Committee on Friday that this year's cereals crop is between 200 and 205 million tonnes, a Commission official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not drawn up a detailed calculation but the crop is put by our officials at between 200 and 205 million tonnes,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The advisory committee will discuss the balance sheet for the current marketing year.</p>
<p>It will also discuss regulations affecting penalties for durum wheat producers which are due to be considered by EU farm ministers.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be a fairly routine meeting. There is nothing controversial on the agenda,&quot; the official added. --Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
